EXT. PIER AMUSEMENT ARCADE - NIGHT

Neon, salt air, the electronic bleat of a hundred machines. A claw crane glows at the end of a row.

NOVELLA "NOVA" ABIOLA-HARTLEY (20s, sequined jacket) feeds quarters into the crane. Her friend FELICITY "FLISS" OKONJO-VARGA (20s, cardigan, two ice creams) hovers behind. A stranger, WYNDHAM TIERNEY-ASARE (20s, windbreaker, a tin of tokens), waits for the machine.

She presses the stick. The claw descends. It grips a plush octopus. It lifts. It drops it.

She groans and slaps the glass. He stifles a laugh. She turns on him.

NOVA
Don't.

WYNDHAM
I didn't.

NOVA
You were going to.

WYNDHAM
I was going to say nice try.

He slides a token into the slot. Their eyes meet. She steps aside. He takes the stick. The claw descends over the octopus. Fliss licks her ice cream. Watches them both.

The claw grabs. Lifts. Shakes. The octopus swings and holds, then drops into the chute. It tumbles out.

He picks it up. Hands it to Nova. She takes it.

NOVA
Thank you.

WYNDHAM ^
You're welcome.

They speak at once and laugh. Fliss clears her throat.

FLISS
(to Nova)
We're going to miss the Ferris wheel.

NOVA
(to Fliss)
Go on. I'll catch up.

Fliss shrugs. Goes. Nova turns to Wyndham, hugging the octopus.

NOVA (CONT'D)
So.

WYNDHAM
So.

She looks at the octopus. He looks at his shoes. A siren whoops from a driving game and someone shouts jackpot. She starts to speak and the lights on the pier go out.

Darkness. A collective moan from the arcade. A beat. Then the lights return, brighter than before, and he is gone. She is alone with the octopus.

She looks around. Down the row, by the Ferris wheel entrance, he is waving. Her ticket is in his hand.
